<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR mostly steady ahead of auction.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR mostly steady ahead of auction.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were mostly unchanged on Monday ahead of the Treasury bill auction later in the day, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;Bankers are usually cautious on Monday. They adjust their PHIBOR rates according to the T-bill rates,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Traders were expecting an increase in T-bill auction rates after the yield curve flattened last week.</p>
<p>Only the one- and two-week rates slipped slightly.</p>
<p>PHIBOR are average swap rates offered by 20 banks in the country.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			 JUNE 16		 JUNE 13</p>
<p>    1 W		12  1/4		 12  5/16</p>
<p>    2 W		12			12  1/8</p>
<p>    1 M		11  3/8		 11  3/8</p>
<p>    2 M		11  3/8		 11  3/8</p>
<p>    3 M		11  7/16		11  7/16</p>
<p>    6 M		11  7/16		11  7/16</p>
<p>    12M		11  3/8		 11  3/8</p>
<p>    VAL		17-Jun		  16-Jun</p>
